body: |-
  What shipped (builder: Kit):
  - 21 counted build-time patches plus 5 import stand-ins strip the engine's fonts, eval-class and WebAssembly source, data: URLs, inline styles, hardcoded hosts and the stock Library. Each patch is pinned to the engine file's sha256 and a measured match count.
  - Board chunk 1,523,875 bytes of a 4,194,304 budget, inside the single GUI tree hash; `--check` fails closed on an unpinned, changed or oversized file. The build is byte-identical on macOS, Windows and Ubuntu.
  - The CSP rule bytes (rules.ts:45-58) are pinned by test and unchanged. Nothing was loosened.
  - Root npm overrides (nanoid 3.3.20, lodash-es 4.18.1, katex 0.19.1, scoped under Excalidraw) bring a fresh install to 0 vulnerabilities.

  Side effect worth more than the milestone: T-2026-11-06-003, the P12 WKWebView failure that kept Gnomon CI red for weeks, is fixed. Cause: the probe's offscreen window made the page `visibilityState: hidden`, so timers ran but requestAnimationFrame never fired and no report was sent. Keeping the page visible fixed it on hosted macos-15 (3 of 3 runs).

  What review found that the builder's own evidence did not:
  - Mika, rendering: select-then-Library raised CSP refusals; board text falls to the default serif; later, that the image tool inserts a broken placeholder with no message rather than refusing.
  - Probe: marks added in the tick the mount resolved were wiped about 20 ms later. The preview fixture was blank while its diagnostics said marks=3; the probe hid it with a 200 ms wait. Also seven paste and drop repros (SVG-as-text becomes an image; clipboard JSON adds an iframe srcdoc; a dropped scene file replaces the board) that now bind S1.3 as condition C8.
  - Judge: per-patch tests asserted a value the code had just assigned; a crash after mount vanished; the GUI embed is inlined three times in the kernel dist (T-2026-11-24-005).
  - Aegis: the audit condition was unmet; a blanket test exemption for board/* replaced with pinned sink counts.
  - CI: Firefox, installed on runners but not on the founder's Mac, rejected the harness's synthetic pointer capture.

  Process notes: the builder hit a 100-turn limit once (milestone too wide for one run); each docs push to the feature branch cancelled the CI run in progress, so no full run completed until pushes stopped; reviewers without a shell still found real defects by reading, and every finding the builder checked reproduced.
